    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="1179" n="1021" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1021"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Emperor of Japan to
                        President Roosevelt</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-06-26"><hi rendition="#italic">June 26,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have just received with great interest and appreciation the kind message sent
                    by you over the cable which has recently been laid between Guam and Japan and
                    which will shortly be open to the public. I am highly gratified to know that the
                    first telegram by this new <pb facs="1180" n="1022" xml:id="pg1022"/> line which
                    united our two countries should convey to me the assurances of the friendly
                    sentiments of the Government and people of the United States for myself and my
                    people. I most cordially reciprocate your expressions of good will and good
                    wishes.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mutsuhito.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
